h Hearts)** provides flush potential (~6.5% chance to make a flush by river)\n- **Ace-6 suited** is considered a playable hand, especially in heads-up play\n- Position matters, but since I can check, I'm likely in the big blind\n\n**Promising moves:**\n\n1. **Check (0)**: Free card to see the flop. Low risk, preserves chips, good for speculative hands. Since we can see a flop for free, this is valuable.\n\n2. **Raise to 200-400**: Shows strength, could take down the pot immediately if opponent has a weak hand. However, risks more chips with a marginal holding.\n\n3. **Fold (-1)**: Too conservative. A6 suited has decent equity in heads-up play and we can see the flop for free.\n\n4. **All-in (-2)**: Extremely aggressive with a marginal hand. Unnecessary risk this early in the match (only hand 4/20).\n\n**Reason:**\n\nSince I can **check for free** (I'm in the big blind and opponent hasn't raised), I should definitely see the flop. A6 suited has:\n- Reasonable showdown value\n- Flush draw potential  \n- Straight possibilities (wheel potential with A-2-3-4-5)\n- Ace-high often wins in heads-up\n\nThere's no reason to fold a playable hand when I can see the flop without additional investment. Raising would be unnecessarily aggressive with a marginal hand when I can gather more information cheaply.\n\n**Answer: 0**"}
