but not a monster. A value bet of around 1000 chips allows me to extract value from worse Ace-high hands (A-K, A-J, etc.) while not overcommitting if they surprisingly have me beat. This bet size maintains fold equity against bluffs while getting called by hands I beat. Given I'm slightly behind in chips and need to win, checking would be too passive with such a strong hand.\n\nAnswer: 1000"}
